        "y": 25
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Batch latency is received-to-flushed. Sustained growth in pending entries means flushing is backlogged. A flat flush rate while traffic arrives means writes are not landing. Rising flush duration points at object store latency or undersized ingestion. Permits in use pinned at max means writes are queuing. [Ingestion](https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/self-host-smithdb-metrics#ingestion)"
      }
    },
